# Staff / Payroll people-ops boundary

## Product role

The **HR & Staff** tab is a **people-ops** sector: register staff, hours, confirm pay
(PAYG / Super / Net), Mark Paid, employee self-service. It is **not** a second cash
engine alongside bank PDF parsing.

## Invariant

On timesheet / payslip **approve**:

- Create **accrual** journals only: wages/super expense + PAYG / Super /
  `LIABILITY_WAGES_PAYABLE` (net).
- **Never** credit `ASSET_CASH` on approve (legacy rows may still exist — detect via
  `isLegacyPayrollCashCredit`).

Cash leaves the business when the **bank statement** shows the transfer. Later
phases match bank outflows to clear wages/PAYG/super payables so Staff totals and
bank spend stay consistent without double P&L expense.

## Do

- Employee enters hours **or clocks in/out**; admin approves and Mark Paid after transfer.
- Keep Staff preview totals (`pay-run-summary`) aligned with payslip status.
- Use **Pay Run (batch)** for period preview → multi-approve; single Timesheet Approval remains.
- **Remittance & ABA**: export Direct Entry `.aba` for approved nets; track PAYG/Super
  due vs bank clears. STP/SuperStream remain external.
- **Payslip email**: mailto summary only (no server SMTP in OSS MVP).
- Attendance open shifts must not count toward pay until clock-out (or cancel).
- Admin can view/edit attendance on the employee **Attendance** tab.
- Salaried staff: set `payBasis: salary` + `salaryAmount`; use Fixed salary Pay Run
  to create submitted timesheets, then batch-approve.
- Persist ABA funding settings via `lib/payroll/aba-settings` (localStorage).
- Heal legacy `ASSET_CASH` payroll credits with the Legacy payroll heal panel.
- When classifying bank wages, prefer liability clearing / match over a second
  `EXPENSE_WAGES` when a Pay Run already accrued the cost (Phase 4+).

## Do not

- Treat approve as “money already left the bank”.
- Import Staff payroll modules into the storefront homepage app.
- Count open (no clock-out) attendance toward Gross / timesheet drafts.
